          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="p-3 sm:p-4 font-mono">IDR 250,000,001 &ndash; IDR 500,000,000</td>
            <td class="p-3 sm:p-4 font-semibold">25%</td>
            <td class="p-3 sm:p-4">~$15,601 &ndash; $31,250 USD</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="p-3 sm:p-4 font-mono">IDR 500,000,001 &ndash; IDR 5,000,000,000</td>
            <td class="p-3 sm:p-4 font-bold text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400">30%</td>
            <td class="p-3 sm:p-4">~$31,251 &ndash; $312,500 USD</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="p-3 sm:p-4 font-mono">Above IDR 5,000,000,000</td>
            <td class="p-3 sm:p-4 font-bold text-red-600 dark:text-red-400">35%</td>
            <td class="p-3 sm:p-4">Above ~$312,500 USD</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <p>
      To see how these marginal brackets apply to your specific monthly or annual salary, use our <a href="/countries/indonesia/income-tax/income-tax-calculator/" class="text-link font-semibold hover:underline">Indonesia Income Tax Calculator</a> for instant net take-home computations.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-on-primary mt-10">
      How Can Bali Digital Nomads Remain 100% Tax Compliant?
    </h2>
    <p>
      Digital nomads can maintain complete tax and legal compliance in Indonesia by adhering to a clear four-step strategy:
    </p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-3">
      <li>
        <strong>Monitor Physical Presence (The 180-Day Rule):</strong> If you do not intend to become an Indonesian tax resident, limit your cumulative stay to under 183 days in any 12-month rolling window. Many remote workers follow a 5-month stay in Bali followed by travel elsewhere in Southeast Asia.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Never Bill Indonesian Clients Directly on an E33G Visa:</strong> Generating domestic income in rupiah from Indonesian businesses or individuals constitutes unlawful employment under immigration regulations and triggers immediate local PPh 21/PPh 23 tax assessments.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Utilize Bilateral Double Taxation Agreements (DTAs):</strong> Indonesia has over 70 DTAs. If you are a tax resident of the UK, US, Australia, or Germany, ensure you obtain a Certificate of Fiscal Residence (CoR) from your home jurisdiction to prevent paying double taxes.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Formalize Your Stay via KITAS if Settling Permanently:</strong> If you intend to establish permanent residency in Indonesia, transition from the E33G to an Investor KITAS (E28A) or Working KITAS (E23), register for an NPWP, and submit your annual SPT Tahunan before March 31.
      </li>
    </ul>

